---
import '../styles/global.css';

const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="What is Akipoly? The property-trading board game, rebuilt for the screen and the new generation — on Arc, with your friends. The short, honest explainer."
    />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#FFF500" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/icons/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/icons/favicon-16.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/icons/favicon-32.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="48x48" href="/icons/favicon-48.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icons/apple-touch-icon.png" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Chango&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="/docs" />
    <title>Akipoly — What is this thing?</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <main id="main" class="docs">
      <div class="docs__top">
        <a class="docs__back" href="/">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 3 6 9l6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
          </svg>
          Back to the site
        </a>
        <a class="docs__wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Akipoly — back to the site">
          <img src="/icons/akipoly-head@96.png" width="34" height="32" alt="" />
          <span>AKIPOLY</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <p class="docs__tldr">
        TL;DR: the property-trading board game. On Arc. With your friends. That's the whole pitch.
      </p>

      <h1 class="docs__title">WHAT IS<br />AKIPOLY?</h1>

      <section class="docs__section" aria-labelledby="docs-what">
        <h2 id="docs-what">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          Akipoly is the property-trading board game, rebuilt for the screen. The same
          dice-rolling, street-snapping, rent-collecting chaos you know and love, moved into a
          fast, loud, playful digital experience built on Arc.
        </p>
        <p>
          It was never about the cardboard. It was the people: the backstabs, the alliances
          that last one round, the trade you brag about for months. Akipoly keeps the social
          engine and leaves the missing pieces and the family feuds about the rules.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs__section" aria-labelledby="docs-how">
        <h2 id="docs-how">So what do you actually do?</h2>
        <p>
          You roll the dice. You buy streets. You build your empire. You bankrupt your friends
          (or they bankrupt you). It's the same triangle it has always been:
        </p>
        <ul class="docs__list">
          <li><strong>BUY</strong> — claim your place on the board.</li>
          <li><strong>BUILD</strong> — turn your moves into an empire.</li>
          <li><strong>COMPETE</strong> — challenge your friends and win loudly.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>No lengthy rulebook required. You know the game. We know you know the game.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs__section" aria-labelledby="docs-arc">
        <h2 id="docs-arc">Wait. Why Arc?</h2>
        <p>
          Because on Arc, this isn't just a game you play, it's a place you play through. Your
          properties, your pieces and your wins are recorded on Arc, the chain Akipoly calls
          home. Bought is bought. No landlord's spreadsheet reaches here.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs__section" aria-labelledby="docs-who">
        <h2 id="docs-who">Who is this for?</h2>
        <p>
          People who have ever flipped a board. People who collect things on the internet.
          People who want bragging rights, no meetings, and exactly three apologies per session.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs__section" aria-labelledby="docs-when">
        <h2 id="docs-when">When does it launch?</h2>
        <p>
          When it's ready — no fake dates, no manufactured suspense. The waitlist hears first,
          because that's what the waitlist is for. If you want to know the moment the dice are
          warm, that's the door.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs__section" aria-labelledby="docs-fine-print">
        <h2 id="docs-fine-print">The fine print</h2>
        <p>
          Akipoly is an independent project, built from scratch, in the spirit of the classic
          property-trading board game. It is not affiliated with any classic board game or its
          publisher. Artwork and everything else here is original.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="docs__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--lg" href="/">Join the waitlist</a>
      </div>

      <p class="page__legal">
        © {year} Akipoly. All rights reserved.<br />
        Akipoly is an independent project, not affiliated with any classic board game or its publisher.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
